.nh
.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-schedule-create - Create a scheduled job (cron, every N minutes or once)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container schedule create   (--cron EXPR | --every DURATION | --at TIME) (--service NAME [-- COMMAND...] | --url URL) [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a command of a service (as a one-off job: the image of the running version, its variables and secrets) or
calls a URL on a schedule. Times follow --timezone (default Europe/Istanbul). A run never starts while the previous
run of the same schedule is still going. Failed runs can be retried (--retries 0-3); after the last attempt you get
a schedule_failed notification (and schedule_missed when a run could not start in time). Free on node plans; on
Serverless each run is billed like a task. Limits: shortest interval 1 minute (Serverless 5), schedules per
environment 5-10 by plan (see "gyro limits").


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--at\fP=""
	run once at this time: 2026-12-01T03:00 (in --timezone) or RFC 3339

.PP
\fB--body\fP=""
	HTTP body (text, or @file)

.PP
\fB--cpu\fP=""
	vCPU of a run (default: same as the service)

.PP
\fB--cron\fP=""
	cron expression: minute hour day month weekday, e.g. "0 3 * * \fI" (daily 03:00), "\fP/15 * * * *", "0 9 * * 1-5"; @daily / @hourly work too

.PP
\fB--description\fP=""
	description

.PP
\fB--every\fP=0s
	run every N minutes instead of a cron expression, e.g. 15m, 2h (at least 1m; Serverless 5m)

.PP
\fB--header\fP=[]
	HTTP header "Name: value" (repeatable; values are kept secret)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--http-timeout\fP=0s
	time limit of the HTTP call (1s-120s, default 30s)

.PP
\fB--memory\fP=0
	memory in MB of a run (default: same as the service)

.PP
\fB--method\fP=""
	HTTP method (default GET)

.PP
\fB--paused\fP[=false]
	create it paused

.PP
\fB--retries\fP=0
	retries after a failed run, 0-3 (30 s × attempt apart)

.PP
\fB--service\fP=""
	run the command after "--" with this service's image, variables and secrets

.PP
\fB--time-limit\fP=0s
	stop a run after this time (10s-6h, default 30m)

.PP
\fB--timezone\fP=""
	IANA time zone of the schedule (default Europe/Istanbul), e.g. UTC

.PP
\fB--url\fP=""
	call this URL instead (http:// or https://)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--account\fP=""
	act in another account you are a panel user of (id from \fBgyro account list\fR; "self" = your own; env GYRO_ACCOUNT, profile default: \fBgyro account use\fR)

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gyro container schedule create 17000 nightly-report --cron "0 3 * * *" --service api -- npm run report
  gyro container schedule create 17000 queue-clean --every 15m --service worker --retries 2 -- php artisan queue:prune-failed
  gyro container schedule create 17000 ping-app --every 5m --url https://example.com/cron --method POST --header "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
  gyro container schedule create 17000 campaign --at 2026-12-01T09:00 --service api -- node send.js
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgyro-container-schedule(1)\fP
